# Access Control (RBAC + ABAC)

- Roles are defined in the domain with business semantics (`Auditor`, `Tutor`, `Admin`) — not generic strings
- The permission matrix is explicitly documented per action × role
- Beyond role (RBAC), access may depend on contextual attributes (ABAC): e.g., a clinic only sees an animal currently under its care
- Authorization is verified in the Application layer **before** any domain operation
- In multi-tenant systems, tenant isolation is verified on **every** request — no exceptions

## Permission Matrix

Document every protected action with required role(s) and attribute conditions before implementation.
